<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Toronto Parks &mdash; OSM Coverage Gaps Over Time</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../index.css">
<style>
  main { max-width: 900px; }
  .legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1.1rem; font-size: .9rem; margin: 1rem 0 .25rem; }
  .legend span { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .4rem; }
  .legend i { display: inline-block; width: 18px; height: 0; border-top: 2px solid; border-radius: 2px; }
  .legend .attic i { width: 14px; height: 12px; border: 0; background: var(--code-bg); }
  .chart { position: relative; overflow-x: auto; }
  .chart svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; font-size: 12px; }
  .chart .attic-band { fill: var(--code-bg); }
  .chart .grid { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; }
  .chart .axis { fill: var(--muted); }
  .chart .series { fill: none; stroke-width: 2; stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: round; }
  .chart .pt { stroke: #fff; stroke-width: 2; }
  .chart .end-label { fill: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .chart .crosshair { stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 1; pointer-events: none; }
  .chart .hit { fill: transparent; cursor: crosshair; }
  .tip {
    position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; pointer-events: none; display: none;
    background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.12); padding: .45rem .65rem;
    font-size: .85rem; line-height: 1.45; white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .tip .d { color: var(--muted); }
  .tip i { display: inline-block; width: 12px; border-top: 2px solid; margin-right: .4rem; vertical-align: middle; }
  .tip strong { display: inline-block; min-width: 3em; }
  .empty { color: var(--muted); padding: 2rem 0; }
  table.runs { font-size: .9rem; }
  table.runs th { width: auto; }
  table.runs td:not(:first-child):not(:last-child) { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
</style>
<script defer src="history.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
<main>

<h1>OSM coverage gaps over time</h1>
<p class="lead">
  How many City of Toronto parks are still <strong>missing</strong> from
  OpenStreetMap, mapped under a <strong>different name</strong>, or mapped as an
  <strong>unnamed</strong> area &mdash; one point per weekly comparison, so a
  mapper can see the worklist shrink.
</p>
<p class="meta">{{RUN_COUNT}} comparisons since {{FIRST_DATE}} &middot; last {{BUILD_DATE}} &middot;
  <a href="./">current gaps</a> &middot; <a href="history.jsonl">data (JSONL)</a></p>

<div class="legend" id="legend"></div>
<div class="chart" id="chart"><div class="tip" id="tip"></div></div>

<p class="meta" style="margin-top:.75rem">
  Points in the shaded span are reconstructed after the fact from OSM's own
  history (an Overpass attic query for that date, compared against today's
  City polygons); the rest were observed by the weekly build. Counts follow
  the City's Green Spaces dataset, so they move when the City adds or
  reclassifies parks, not only when someone maps one.
</p>

<h2>Every comparison</h2>
<table class="runs">
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Date</th><th>Missing</th><th>Mismatch</th><th>Unnamed</th><th>TRCA</th>
        <th>City polygons</th><th>OSM areas</th><th>Source</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
{{HISTORY_ROWS}}
  </tbody>
</table>

<p class="meta" style="margin-top:2rem">
  Built by <a href="https://github.com/{{GITHUB_REPO}}">{{GITHUB_REPO}}</a>.
  OSM data &copy; <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap contributors</a>.
</p>

<script type="application/json" id="history-data">{{HISTORY_JSON}}</script>
</main>
</body>
</html>
